# SPIDER's five tracks (pattern.h NTRK) and its engines (dsp/synth_spider.c): a new project is the kit, poly, mono,
# acid and samples (slice). Away from Steps the top row mutes T1-T5, then pad 6 the throws (held, the conductor), pad
# 7 FX I's return, pad 8 FX II's (seq.mute's bits: engine.c mutes the returns); FADER BANK: T5, FX I, FX II, the master
wait 300
expect par1.0 5
expect par2.0 0
expect par3.0 1
expect par4.0 2
expect par5.0 4
expect par3.vmode 1
expect par4.vmode 2
tap HOME
expect page Arrange
expect mute 0
tappad 4
expect mute 16
tappad 4
expect mute 0
# pad 6: tapped, the throws; held, the conductor
tappad 5
expect mute 64
tappad 5
expect mute 0
pad 5 100
wait 600
pad 5 0
wait 40
expect mute 32
pad 5 100
wait 600
pad 5 0
wait 40
expect mute 0
# pads 7 and 8: the returns
tappad 6
expect mute 128
tappad 7
expect mute 384
shot tracks_mutes.png
tappad 6
tappad 7
expect mute 0
# the faders' second bank
smktap FADERBANK
fader 1 64
fader 1 100
expect par8.level 100
fader 2 64
fader 2 90
expect par9.level 90
fader 0 64
fader 0 80
expect par5.level 80
# the Mix page: five strips and the two returns
tap GLO
shot tracks_mix.png
# the keybed plays on Steps (the pads are its cells there): a white key on a synth track sounds
tap HOME
turn ALGO 1
wait 200
wav keys_on_steps.wav
key 7 down 100
wait 300
key 7 up
wait 100
wavstop
